Privacy Policy
In short: Antibiotic does not collect, store on our servers, share or sell any personal data. The game works fully offline and keeps your progress only on your own device.

1. Who we are
“Antibiotic: Germ Survivor” (also published as “Antibiyotik”, the “Game”) is developed and published by Vainsteel Studios, Ankara, Türkiye (“we”, “us”). This policy applies to the Game on iOS, iPadOS and Android.

2. Data we collect
We do not collect any personal data. The Game has no account system, no sign-in, no advertising and no analytics or tracking tools. We do not collect your name, e-mail address, phone number, contacts, location, photos, device identifiers or advertising identifiers.

3. Data stored on your device
Game progress and settings (levels, in-game currency, items, looks, sound and language settings) are saved only in the Game's local storage on your device. They are never sent to us.
Optional gameplay statistics (for example number of sessions and play time) are kept only on your device, are never sent automatically, and can be turned off and deleted in the Game under My game data.
Backup and report files are created only when you tap “Save progress backup” or “Save report”. The file is saved through your device's share sheet to a place you choose; you decide whether to share it with anyone.
4. In-app purchases
Optional in-app purchases are processed entirely by the Apple App Store or Google Play under their own terms and privacy policies. We never receive your name, payment card or billing details. The Game only receives a confirmation that a purchase was completed so it can add the purchased item to the save data on your device.

Apple Privacy Policy: apple.com/legal/privacy
Google Privacy Policy: policies.google.com/privacy

5. Sharing and selling of data
Because we do not collect personal data, we do not share, sell or rent any personal data to third parties, and we do not use your data for advertising or profiling.

6. Internet access and permissions
The Game does not need an internet connection to play. A connection is used only by the Apple App Store or Google Play when you view prices, make a purchase or restore purchases. The Game does not request access to your camera, microphone, location, contacts or photos.

7. Children
The Game is suitable for a general audience and does not knowingly collect personal data from anyone, including children under 13 (or the equivalent minimum age in your country). Parents can use the parental controls of their device to manage in-app purchases.

8. Data retention and deletion
All game data stays on your device until you delete it. You can delete it at any time by deleting the Game or clearing its data in your device settings. Deleting the Game also deletes your progress, so save a backup first if you want to keep it. Purchases of the Supporter Pack can be restored with “Restore purchases” in the Shop.

9. Your rights
Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal data. Since we do not hold any personal data about you, there is normally nothing for us to access or delete, but you are welcome to contact us with any question.

10. Not medical advice
The Game is entertainment only. Its medical and biological theme is fictional and it does not provide medical information, diagnosis or treatment advice.

11. Changes to this policy
If we change this policy (for example if a future version adds new features), we will update this page and the effective date above before the change takes effect.

